\f1\fs22 St Hedges Cathedral singularly proved that the thinking processes of the Airborne didn't always draw the straightest line between the itch of greed and the quick return of profit. The cathedral and its environs was undoubtably the costliest capital expenditure project in the history of the Great Meritocracy of Ulyssia. Ostentatious, stately, awe-inspiring, and a triumph of engineering\'97these were just some of superlatives used to describe the cathedral's bathrooms.\
The cathedral itself existed on another plane of grandeur altogether.\
This is how the rich immortalise themselves.\
It covered more than 10 hectares in area, more than 1 billion square centimetres, because the venture capitalists who sat on the board of St Hedges Permanent Holdings and Stranglings LLC demanded at least one measurement of its grandiosity should exceed 1 billion somethings.\
At each of the nine corners of the platform, a statue of one of the Nine Major Saints of Latter Day Capitalism looked out, valiant and imposing, over the sun-drenched cerulean skies. They saw all who came and went, each guarding a hover-pad stuck to the platform like a huge grey, stale lollipop.\
The dead saints watch you arrive. The dead saints watch you leave.\
At the centre of the platform, St Hedges presided over spectacular sweeping lawns and beds of flowers framed by topiaries of geometrically trimmed hedges and imposing copses of trees. The flower beds were of all the most extraordinary colours of the rainbow except red, which was, of course, an unwelcome colour, representing bad news in politics, or on any financial report. Following the same construct of good and evil, the lawns were all black, representing perennial profit, and the death of socialism.\
Black grass, you say? True! Horticulturalists were hired to cultivate a new breed of grass, the colour of which was aptly called Accountancy Black.\
This is how power rewrites nature.\
Wide, sweeping stone paths curved through the grounds and converged on the cathedral, which both inspired and conquered the fiscal souls of all who approached. Incorporating advanced metallurgy for the structure, and brutalist masonry for the facades of limestone and bluestone, it was its clever use of glass ceilings which invariably struck a first-time visitor dumb.\
Everything about the cathedral and its environs was designed to impress. No expense in the construction and detailing of the cathedral was spared because every Airborne knew, in the warm cockles of their wallets and purses, an impressed person was a distracted person, and a distracted person was easier to rob.\
The floors of the cathedral nave were paved in the most flawless marble, the pews hewn from the most endangered of hardwoods, and the pew cushions for easing the aches of the richest arses were reportedly made of the luxurious hides of mink. Or perhaps seal. Both kinds of farmed animal had been genetically engineered to grow plump, square and cushion-shaped.\
This is how extinction serves comfort.\
Adorning the walls were graphs and tables inlaid with precious jewels and metals that glinted, scintillated and coruscated as they caught light from the windows and the bling of congregations. If the light was right, the trend lines and numbers of key holy indicators such as customer acquisition cost, customer lifetime value, recurring revenue, churn rate, and net promoter score seemed to leap off the walls and come alive.\
The actual seating capacity of the nave is Commercial in Confidence, but has been estimated in various financial markets to be somewhere between 3000 and 23 billion. Curiously, no one has ever bothered to count the seats, but the St Hedges Cathedral Preservation Society consistently boasts, in their annual reports, a seating capacity growth rate of 23% year-on-year. No one actually believes this, but the mere publication of the numbers seems sufficient to ward off disgruntled investors and hostile take-overs.\
This is how lies become truth through repetition.\
Whether the cathedral seated 3000 or 23 billion, the congregation attending the holy joint venture of Alexander Shakti and Sarah Jacobson were too few to suffocate all the plump, square platypus cushions, even as their arse cheeks were privilege-flabby. Initially, Alexander's side of the aisle made a better show of it, but that was mainly due to the number of production crews working every angle of the ceremony.\
Sarah's side of the nave was barely one third full. That is, until the Elvi showed up.\
Curiously, many of the Elvi were carrying in their arms, bundles of light fabric and tangles of ropes that could have been parachutes. Despite apparently parachute-crashing the exclusive ceremony, all their hair was perfect.\
The younger Airborne attendees, being fans of the overnight success of Elvi music, were enraptured by the mass appearance of their cultural heroes. Cries of, 'We love you, Elvi', 'I want to have your babies', and 'Sing Evolve Me Tender' disrupted the decorum of the solemn mood. Older, more conservative Airborne would have nothing of such an offensive intrusion by lazy, low-class minimum-wage-abusers, and with dismissive waves of angry protest, filed out of the pews towards the exits.\
Alexander panicked; the status of his moment in the sun was draining, so he did what he did best: he flashed a gormless expression of confusion at his senior associate producer, who quickly understood the non-verbal plea: For tax's sake, fix this!\
This is how you manipulate a crowd.\
The associate producer ordered all cameras on site be aimed like weapons at the fleeing Airborne. Faced with the probability of a blitz of unflattering coverage at the hands of Alexander's publicity machine, most considered what a shame it would be to miss the reception afterwards, and returned to their seats.\
The Elvi continued to file in until all remaining seat cushions were flattened, and the event became standing room only, which is to say the marketing department could plausibly claim the crowd numbered more than 23 billion.\
Among the invited dignitaries in the second row, Piotr Dunhilton clenched his jaw with determination as the tides of Airborne and Elvi ebbed and flowed. With narrow eyes he watched Sarah, whose countervailing fear and exhilaration made theatre of her face. She brushed a tear from her eye and smiled. Dunhilton thought he saw relief in the way she exhaled and tension melted from her shoulders. In the soft curl of her gentle smile and the flushing of her cheeks, he thought he saw affection. Sarah Jacobson had affection for these clones. Dunhilton saw her affection and didn't like it.\
This is how control begins to slip away.\
With apoplexy, the Very Arch Bishop of Business of Ulyssia, Ignatius d'Molesto, watched the mob sweating in his cathedral, and lamented the inadequacy of the security he had bought for the event. With resignation, he huffed and sighed from his very comfortable, well-cushioned throne.\
the High Elvis entered the nave to cheers from his flock, strode up the aisle and stood before the Very Arch Bishop. They regarded each other and, when the High Elvis realised the Bishop would not vacate the throne for him, he turned and stood proudly at the right side.\
At precisely that moment, sunlight poured through the stained glass windows and fell just so, reflecting off the precious jewels and metals in all the graphs and tables etched into the walls of the nave. By an incalculable accident of geometry, much of the reflected light struck pinpoints in the sunglasses and jewellery of the High Elvis, and from there shone on the congregation with the intensity of a thousand mirror balls in a thousand nightclubs.\
The Elvi gazed upon the spectacle with awe and amazement, and knew beyond a certainty it was a sign. As one, they took to their feet, enfolded their arms in the manner of cradling a newborn baby, and chanted, 'Holy Momma! Holy Momma!'\
You watch a cult being born in real time. You witness the moment myth becomes reality.\
Dunhilton became all the more alarmed as the chanting rang out and the very pregnant Sarah smiled with embarrassment. Dunhilton realised she was accepting the title as hers. Sarah Jacobson is the Holy Momma!\
The earth turned and rolled along its orbit, the sunbeams tilted, and the High Elvis was no longer cast as a being of light. He stepped forward and waved the Elvi chanting down. When reverent silence had been restored, the Very Arch Bishop rose and pompously strode to the pulpit to begin the ceremony, taking the utmost care that his robes swished perfectly.\
the High Elvis nicked his seat.\
This is how power transitions. This is how thrones are stolen.\
The Very Arch Bishop d'Molesto addressed the congregation.\
'Dearly invested, we are gathered here today, in sight of the Nine Major Saints of Latter Day Capitalism, to witness and celebrate the exchange of contracts between these two counter parties, Sarah Jacobson and Alexander Shakti, in the matter of holy joint venture. We praise the perfection of the Market and render up our forecasts in thanks-giving, trusting they will always be truer than throwing a dart at a board. May your enterprises be always too big to fail.'\
'And also yours.'\
'And I say unto you, it is easier for a camel to pass through the security checkpoint of an investment bank than it is for a rich person to allow a poor person a dollar.'\
'They don't deserve it.'\
The Very Arch Bishop opened the extremely heavy bible and scowled, mildly annoyed that he needed to flick a few pages forward and back to find his place. He usually nailed the right page for scripture readings as common as these.\
'From the New Ulyssian Market Bible, the first reading is from Exploitations, Chapter 1.\
'In the beginning, the Market created the heavens and the earth, and the Market moved over the earth. Then the Market said, "Let there be privilege"; and there was privilege. The Market saw that privilege was good, and separated the privileged from under-privileged.\
'Then the Market said, "Let Us cast humanity in Our image, according to Our perfection; and let them exploit the fish and the birds and the cattle and every creeping thing."\
'The Market moulded humanity in Its own image, in the image of the Market It moulded them, into the chosen and the reviled. And to the chosen the Market said, "Go forth and multiply your assets; fill the earth and subdue it; rule over every living thing, and exploit every resource I have given you. Cut and burn and extract and consume all I have given you."'\
'May your taxes be small and your margins large,' the Airborne in the congregation chanted. The Elvi sat dumbfounded, soaking up every nuance of the ritual as if it was life-giving elixir.\
This is how you program obedience. This is how you sanctify greed.\
'And from St Rupert's 2nd email to the Corinthians, Chapter 5: "Therefore anyone of the Market is a new creature; old indiscretions are buried and forgotten; behold, fresh opportunities arise."\
'And finally from St Rupert's 1st email to the Corinthians, Chapter 13: "The Market is impatient; the Market is ruthless and jealous; the Market brags and is arrogant. It is easily provoked, keeps account for wrongs suffered, rejoices in quick wins, and kicks truth down the road. It bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, exploits all things."\
The Very Arch Bishop closed the bible; the Airborne in the congregation fondled their jewellery; the Elvi combed their hair and straightened their sunglasses.\
The Bishop came down from the pulpit and stood before the happy couple, saying, 'Sarah and Alexander, will you honour the sacred charge of joint venturers, and together seal and harden your resolve for profit, in prosperity and tax audit, in price gouging and cashflow crisis?'\
'We will.'\
'And now for the exchanging of cheques.'\
The was a brief pause while Sarah elbowed Alexander, prompting him to recite his lines.\
'With this cheque, I, Alexander Shakti, take you, Sarah Jacobson, as my lawfully contracted counter party in holy joint venture, to have and to hold accountable, for better or much better, for richer or even richer, for as long as we both remain solvent.'\
Restrained, self-entitled tittering could be heard among the congregation; no Airborne ever became insolvent.\
After a pregnant pause, Sarah placed a small poly-paper cheque in Alexander's hand and said, 'Yeah, me too.'\
'Let the cheques be cashed,' declared Bishop d'Molesto, as the happy couple folded their cheques into gold wallets. 'I now pronounce you joint venturers. You may celebrate the deal.'\
This is how capitalism replaces love. This is how wealth marries wealth.\
When Alexander lifted the black veil and revealed Sarah's face, everyone held their breaths in collective awe and joy. It was later agreed no one had seen a lovelier, healthier counter party.\
Alexander shook with nerves, yet steadied enough to lean in and peck Sarah's lips. He was already anticipating how good he'd look in the celebration vids with Sarah on his arm.\
The congregation rose and applauded.\
The Elvi cheered and began singing. Their hips swayed and there was not a dry eye behind their dark sunglasses. 'All praise the Holy Momma of the New Church of the One After the One!' they declared.\
'Praise the Holy Momma!' they chanted over and over.\
Dunhilton dug his fingernails deep into the varnish of the pew in front of him.\
'Praise the Holy Momma!'\
Dunhilton's knuckles turned white as he stared threats of dismemberment at the Very Arch Bishop.\
Bishop d'Molesto was struck to the core with fear.\
This is how a new religion is born. This is how the old order trembles.\
Unable to contain himself, Dunhilton marched on d'Molesto and drew near enough to his ear. 'Do you realise what you've done? You've exposed these clones to religion! Sweet Salt and Vinegar Jesus Chips, doesn't anyone read a warranty card any more?'\

